record(s,t,r,d,inv,'The leaf states symmetry of the CM condition in E and K, abandons a field-of-definition argument in a boxed cancellation, and asserts invariance under extension in the NB. The second live condition visibly uses ⊂ although the following calculation writes equality. Those signs remain distinct as written. Check 148.N1: the coordinate-product identity (g×1)(h×h)=(gh×h)=(1×h)(gh×1) confirms the two-letter gh that survives in the cancelled verification; neither witness retained h there. The other inconsistent primes of that abandoned argument remain where visible. The author labels the last assertion “vérification triviale”; it was transcribed, not independently established here. Archive number 147.',doubts=[['148','cancelled donc',r'\unsure{donc}','Only d and covered low strokes.','low'],['148','word before des',r'\unsure{par}','Partly struck short word.','low'],['148','first inverse in locally struck product',r'\unsure{g^{-1}|g}','Exponent area crossed by other ink.','low'],['148','global stabilizer RHS',r"\unsure{\Sigma'|\Sigma}",'Raised mark overwritten.','low'],['148','two local cancellations',r'\unsure{par ci-dessus};\unsure{gK}','Long and short strokes cover words/letters.','low']],notation=[['Two coordinate actions','τ×1; 1×τ; diagonal τ×τ','148','The second displayed condition uses a curved subset sign.'],['Ideal symbol',r'\mathfrak U','148','All visible occurrences match scan 147.']],hand=['A heavily retraced equality may conceal its earlier form; the two final parallel strokes of (*) are clear.','The h following g in the cancelled product has a tall stem; it was read as a prime by C and omitted by H.','Underlining réciproquement and striking La théorie de Galois are separate strokes on separate baselines; H combines them into one deletion.'],abbreviations=[['Sh. Tan.','Shimura–Taniyama (attribution abbreviated on the sheet)'],['NB','nota bene']],events=[['148.N1','targeted proof check','Coordinate multiplication gives (g×1)(h×h)=(gh×h)=(1×h)(gh×1), confirming the visible gh in the cancelled formula.']],extra='Certainty-only: M0019 and M0020 resolved from the halves. The crossed (g×1)Σ_y=Σ′_y RHS, pour tte conjugaison, the parenthetical independence sentence, cela, La théorie de Galois and On dit que are resolved after inspection; the remaining local doubts are listed above.')
